{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for the image of the line \\( y = 2x + 1 \\) under the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\), we first need to determine the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\). Given that \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) transforms \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) to \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) to \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can express \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) as:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFrom the given transformations, we have the following system of equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us the following equations:\n\n1. \\(2a - b = 9\\)\n2. \\(2c - d = 3\\)\n3. \\(a - 3b = 7\\)\n4. \\(c - 3d = -1\\)\n\nWe solve the first two equations for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\nFrom equation (1): \\(b = 2a - 9\\)\nFrom equation (3): \\(b = \\frac{a - 7}{3}\\)\n\nEquating the two expressions for \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n2a - 9 = \\frac{a - 7}{3}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying through by 3:\n\n\\[\n6a - 27 = a - 7\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms:\n\n\\[\n5a = 20 \\implies a = 4\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 4\\) back into \\(b = 2a - 9\\):\n\n\\[\nb = 2(4) - 9 = 8 - 9 = -1\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1308,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,279,2168,315,279,1555,17767,379,284,220,17,87,488,220,16,1124,8,1212,279,6172,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,44,11035,701,582,1156,1184,311,8253,279,6172,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,44,11035,568,16246,429,1124,11520,10374,13233,90,44,11035,8,28475,1124,11520,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,17,24984,481,16,1124,408,90,5187,2